<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  the body text of a dialog that asks a question and has nothing else in it.

  **the padding here is placing text inside a panel with a 48dp floor.** Material's dialog layout
  gives both the message panel and the custom-view panel `minHeight="48dp"`, and a line of body text
  is about 20dp - so whatever is short leaves the remainder as blank *below* it, where the button
  bar's own 14dp is then added. that is why a one-line question has a band under it taller than the
  question, and why the dialog does not get shorter when a two-line message loses a line: two lines
  still fit inside the floor.

  so the top padding is not decoration. it moves the text down into a box whose height is fixed
  anyway, spending some of the slack above the sentence instead of leaving all of it below. 16dp is
  what Material puts under a title when it places a spacer there, which is the gap this stands in
  for - a custom view gets `titleDividerNoCustom` set to gone.

  **it is deliberately not raised further to close the gap underneath.** doing so buys a smaller gap
  below only by growing the one above, and the two are not worth the same: the space under a title
  is part of how a dialog reads, while the space over its buttons is just leftover.

  **shrinking the button bar's own padding is not the answer either**, though it is the obvious next
  reach. that value is hard-coded as a dimension rather than read from a theme attribute, so the
  only way to change it is to redeclare the name for the whole app - and the dialogs that carry a
  control instead of a sentence never had the floor's leftover under them, so they lose the padding
  outright and their buttons crowd what is above them.

  the appearance is Material's dialog body deliberately: this replaces where the text sits, not how
  it looks, and a dialog whose message was a different size from every other dialog's would be a
  worse bug than the gap.
-->
<TextView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/message"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:paddingHorizontal="24dp"
    android:paddingTop="16dp"
    android:textAppearance="?attr/textAppearanceBodyMedium"
    android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
    tools:text="This setting goes back to its default, as if you had never changed it." />
